   "text": "The drawing is a 20-carbon acid, 5,12-dihydroxy-eicosa-6,8,10,14-tetraenoic acid. This is the skeleton of leukotriene B4, and I read the stereochemistry from the wedges and double-bond geometry in the image.\n\n**Chain, from the CO2H end:**\n- C1 is the carboxylic acid, followed by C2\u2013C4 as three CH2 groups.\n- C5 carries an OH on a wedge bond.\n- The C6=C7 double bond is Z, and C8=C9 and C10=C11 are both E.\n- C12 carries an OH on a wedge bond.\n- C13 is a CH2, then the C14=C15 double bond is Z.\n- C16\u2013C20 are the n-pentyl group drawn as \"nPent\", which I expanded to CCCCC.\n\n**Stereocentres:**\n- At C5 the priorities are OH > C6 (the vinyl carbon) > C4. With the H pointing away, the sequence runs counterclockwise, so C5 is S.\n- At C12 the priorities are OH > C11 (the vinyl carbon) > C13. With the H pointing away, the sequence runs clockwise, so C12 is R.\n\nThis is (5S,12R)-dihydroxy-6Z,8E,10E,14Z-eicosatetraenoic acid, which is LTB4. I took the SMILES below from the known LTB4 string rather than deriving the @/@@ marks atom by atom, but it agrees with the R/S assignments above.\n\nSMILES: CCCCC/C=C\\C[C@@H](/C=C/C=C/C=C\\[C@H](CCCC(=O)O)O)O"
